  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA multiprofile with PCA2000 and avgpool substantially outperforms single-profile RNA, improving accuracy from 0.485 to 0.591 and F1 from 0.464 to 0.573. The key uncertainty is whether a stronger aggregation method, specifically transformer aggregation, can further improve this promising multiprofile RNA setup. config_003 tests this by changing only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the RNA encoder and profile setting fixed. This is the best next experiment because it directly extends the current best configuration, isolates the effect of aggregation, and avoids confounding changes to modality, encoder, or fusion before it is clear whether more complex aggregation is useful."
}

